<h2>An emerging lane, honestly presented</h2>
<p>We have verified trade data showing Brazil as a genuine market for Indian dehydrated onion, and it's the clearest data point we have for Latin American demand. Beyond that specific product and market, our research to date hasn't produced verified, citable figures for other Latin American countries or products — and consistent with how we handle every page on this site, we're not going to publish numbers we can't stand behind.</p>

<h2>That doesn't mean we can't supply the region</h2>
<p>It means we haven't yet built out the research to back a detailed country-by-country guide. If you're a buyer anywhere in Latin America, <a href="/get-a-quote/">send us your requirement</a> — product, quantity, destination port — and we'll quote directly, being upfront about transit time (typically 30–40 days from Indian ports, among the longest routes we serve) and what documentation we can confirm for your specific import.</p>

